				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\varSigma }_{{{{{{\rm{ph}}}}}}}=\frac{{\varPhi }_{{{{{{\rm{ph}}}}}}}}{A}t$$\end{document}Σph=ΦphAtwhere Φph is the incident photon flux (ph s−1), A is the beam spot size on the sample surface (cm2) and t is the total irradiation time (s). Thus, photon irradiance has units of photon cm−2 and is used throughout this work.

